From 81547cab0bbbe1aa6a55bbf329045bfb1636dfeb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Stellman <astellman@stellman-greene.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 10:05:28 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] scsi: target: iscsi: Match NOP-Out replies only against
 NOP-Ins

iscsit_process_nop_out() treats a NOP-Out with the reserved ITT and a
Target Transfer Tag as the reply to an unsolicited NOP-In. It looks the
TTT up with iscsit_find_cmd_from_ttt(), which returns the first command
on conn_cmd_list with that tag whatever its opcode, then sets that
command to ISTATE_REMOVE and queues it for the TX thread to free.

NOP-Ins aren't the only commands with a TTT. READs take theirs from the
same per-session counter, as do Text commands with a pending
continuation, and Rejects allocated by iscsit_add_reject() keep the 0
that iscsit_allocate_cmd() leaves in targ_xfer_tag.

Commit 9547308bda29 ("target/iscsi: Fix double free of a TUR followed by a
solicited NOPOUT") fixed this for non-READ SCSI commands by giving them
a TTT of 0xffffffff, but the lookup can still match these. The counter
starts at 0 for each session, so the TTT of a session's first READ is
known in advance.

If a NOP-Out names the TTT of a READ that the backend is still
processing, the TX thread frees it with transport_generic_free_cmd(),
which doesn't wait for the backend and sets se_cmd->se_lun to NULL.
From reading the code, target_complete_ok_work() then dereferences the
NULL se_lun when the READ completes. I haven't reproduced this on a
running kernel.

Add iscsit_find_nopin_from_ttt(), which matches only NOP-In commands,
and use it for NOP-Out replies. Matching on the opcode after the
existing lookup isn't enough, because a Reject with TTT 0 can be ahead
of a NOP-In that also got TTT 0 on a fresh session. A NOP-Out that names
another command's TTT now closes the connection, as one naming an
unknown TTT already does. iscsit_find_cmd_from_ttt() is unchanged for
its other caller, Data ACK SNACK handling.

The issue was found by Claude Opus 5.5 running Quality Playbook, an
LLM-driven code review tool:
https://github.com/andrewstellman/quality-playbook
The fix and this changelog were drafted with Claude and reviewed by me.

Fixes: e48354ce078c ("iscsi-target: Add iSCSI fabric support for target v4.1")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
---
Not yet run on a kernel. So far it builds with W=1 and no new warnings
(x86_64, ISCSI_TARGET=m), applies cleanly to 7.4/scsi-fixes and
7.5/scsi-staging, and the new lookup, compiled from this patch into a
userspace test, returns the NOP-In ahead of a Reject with the same TTT
and doesn't match READ or Text commands.

A second NOP-Out answering the same NOP-In is still accepted and queues
it for removal twice. That needs a separate change and isn't addressed
here.

 drivers/target/iscsi/iscsi_target.c      |  2 +-
 drivers/target/iscsi/iscsi_target_util.c | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 drivers/target/iscsi/iscsi_target_util.h |  2 ++
 3 files changed, 23 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/target/iscsi/iscsi_target.c b/drivers/target/iscsi/iscsi_target.c
index 124ff269b8e7..e2312799daaf 100644
--- a/drivers/target/iscsi/iscsi_target.c
+++ b/drivers/target/iscsi/iscsi_target.c
@@ -1821,7 +1821,7 @@ int iscsit_process_nop_out(struct iscsit_conn *conn, struct iscsit_cmd *cmd,
 	 * This was a response to a unsolicited NOPIN ping.
 	 */
 	if (hdr->ttt != cpu_to_be32(0xFFFFFFFF)) {
-		cmd_p = iscsit_find_cmd_from_ttt(conn, be32_to_cpu(hdr->ttt));
+		cmd_p = iscsit_find_nopin_from_ttt(conn, be32_to_cpu(hdr->ttt));
 		if (!cmd_p)
 			return -EINVAL;
 
diff --git a/drivers/target/iscsi/iscsi_target_util.c b/drivers/target/iscsi/iscsi_target_util.c
index c1888c42afdd..d4612ff1457e 100644
--- a/drivers/target/iscsi/iscsi_target_util.c
+++ b/drivers/target/iscsi/iscsi_target_util.c
@@ -401,6 +401,26 @@ struct iscsit_cmd *iscsit_find_cmd_from_ttt(
 	return NULL;
 }
 
+struct iscsit_cmd *iscsit_find_nopin_from_ttt(struct iscsit_conn *conn,
+					      u32 targ_xfer_tag)
+{
+	struct iscsit_cmd *cmd;
+
+	spin_lock_bh(&conn->cmd_lock);
+	list_for_each_entry(cmd, &conn->conn_cmd_list, i_conn_node) {
+		if (cmd->iscsi_opcode == ISCSI_OP_NOOP_IN &&
+		    cmd->targ_xfer_tag == targ_xfer_tag) {
+			spin_unlock_bh(&conn->cmd_lock);
+			return cmd;
+		}
+	}
+	spin_unlock_bh(&conn->cmd_lock);
+
+	pr_err("Unable to locate NOPIN TTT: 0x%08x on CID: %u\n",
+	       targ_xfer_tag, conn->cid);
+	return NULL;
+}
+
 int iscsit_find_cmd_for_recovery(
 	struct iscsit_session *sess,
 	struct iscsit_cmd **cmd_ptr,
diff --git a/drivers/target/iscsi/iscsi_target_util.h b/drivers/target/iscsi/iscsi_target_util.h
index 7ae48a8a5cbf..a16b3cef72ad 100644
--- a/drivers/target/iscsi/iscsi_target_util.h
+++ b/drivers/target/iscsi/iscsi_target_util.h
@@ -26,6 +26,8 @@ extern int iscsit_sequence_cmd(struct iscsit_conn *conn, struct iscsit_cmd *cmd,
 extern struct iscsit_cmd *iscsit_find_cmd_from_itt_or_dump(struct iscsit_conn *,
 			itt_t, u32);
 extern struct iscsit_cmd *iscsit_find_cmd_from_ttt(struct iscsit_conn *, u32);
+extern struct iscsit_cmd *iscsit_find_nopin_from_ttt(struct iscsit_conn *conn,
+						     u32 targ_xfer_tag);
 extern int iscsit_find_cmd_for_recovery(struct iscsit_session *, struct iscsit_cmd **,
 			struct iscsi_conn_recovery **, itt_t);
 extern void iscsit_add_cmd_to_immediate_queue(struct iscsit_cmd *, struct iscsit_conn *, u8);

